<p>Nepal’s election commission has released official results showing Balendra Shah’s Rastriya Swatantra Party (RSP) winning 182 seats in the 275-member House of Representatives—enough to form a majority government. Multiple outlets called it a landslide, with Shah—often described as an engineer-turned-rapper-turned-politician—now in position to become Nepal’s next prime minister.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/7xBLpy-Wgz7ecocYCIHAPULxqpkunE57NSNlTAmayIIjJh4hkRrdYAw6fWFccN0o7TfB15EW-yAfscQNrfv3y8NoHl0uNcKbL6cIMtklbx2ifNY2fqcHKafhR1H3XiDEB7PDIoBHd-Y7bOmn8R_Nliw-T0zjqEyRzVq-yMkKFt-kkyKKSS9uEmQJomjEcm3KNIMHuoY' alt='Balendra Shah after official results confirmed his party’s landslide win in Nepal.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Scale of win: DW calls it a huge—and in Nepal’s recent politics, relatively rare—single-party parliamentary majority.</li><li>New party rise: Al Jazeera notes RSP is only four years old and is set to dominate the new parliament with a near two-thirds majority.</li><li>Youth turnout: Gen Z voters helped fuel RSP’s surge, DW reports, pointing to a generational shift in Nepal’s electorate.</li><li>Economic hopes: Firstpost links the big win to expectations of economic revival, framing Shah’s result as a mandate to focus on jobs and growth.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/asia/nepals-final-poll-result-confirms-landslide-for-balendra-shah-amid-hope-for-economic-revival-13989014.html'>Nepal&#x27;s final poll result confirms landslide for Balendra Shah amid hope for economic revival</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/12/ex-rapper-balendra-shah-sweeps-to-power-in-nepal-landslide-election-victory'>Ex-rapper Balendra Shah sweeps to power in Nepal landslide election victory</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-gen-z-buoys-ex‑rapper-s-party-to-landslide-victory/a-76343841'>Nepal: Gen Z buoys ex‑rapper&#x27;s party to landslide victory</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepals-rsp-party-of-balendra-shah-wins-majority-election-commission/article70736058.ece'>The Nepalese election commission releases the official results of the recent election, with Balen Shah&#x27;s Rastriya Swatantra Party winning 182 seats in the 275-member House of Representatives. The result gives the party a majority in the House and places it two seats short of a supermajority.</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>